Q: Find largest and second largest element in a range A: <p>NomeN's solution looks good, except that the two tests in the loop return false if the array is large, because most array elements don't beat the second best found by the iteration. Slight modification of the code can avoid the problem.</p>
<pre class="lang-c prettyprint-override"><code>for (e: all elements) {
 if (e &lt;= second)
   continue;
 if (e &lt;= first) {
   second = e;
   continue;
 }
 second = largest;
 largest = e;
}
</code></pre>
<p>In most iterations, the first test returns true, so that the loop moves to the next iteration immediately. The rest of the code should be rarely executed.</p>
